# Engineering Principles

Follow professional software engineering standards.

## Before changing code

Always inspect the existing implementation first.
Do not rewrite files blindly.
Do not remove working logic.
Do not introduce new dependencies without explaining why.
Do not fake completed features.

## Code quality

- Use TypeScript strictly.
- Prefer small reusable components.
- Avoid huge screen files when logic can be extracted.
- Avoid duplicated business logic.
- Avoid hardcoded URLs, prices, user IDs, and fake locations.
- Keep UI logic separate from API/data logic where possible.
- Use existing services/hooks before creating new ones.
- Keep naming consistent.

## No-op rule

Never leave clickable UI with empty handlers like:

onPress={() => {}}

If a button is not implemented:
- hide it, or
- disable it with explanation, or
- create a TODO with the required implementation.

## Security rule

Frontend role checks are for UX only.
Backend must enforce real access control.

## Data rule

Do not invent data shapes.
Use the API types, shared types, Prisma schema, or existing services.

## Change size

Prefer focused changes.
Do not combine UI redesign, backend refactor, and database migration in one task unless explicitly requested.

## Documentation

For every important change, update or create a short note explaining:
- what changed
- why it changed
- files affected
- how to test